Trial: give OHOS the Linux entries of the GPU lists.

GpuControlList::GetOsType() has no OHOS arm and falls through to kOsAny,
so every entry in the software rendering list and the driver bug list that
names an operating system is inert on this port -- nothing in either list
applies here except the handful that name none.

This maps OHOS to Linux, to see what that turns on and whether anything
breaks. It is a test build, asked for on its own so its effect can be told
apart from anything else.

What should change, read off the 154 lists: 20 Linux entries in the
software rendering list and 28 in the driver bug list, but almost all are
keyed to a desktop vendor or driver (Intel, NVIDIA, AMD, Mesa, VMware,
VirtualBox) and cannot match a phone. Two can:

- 283, no conditions at all: exit_on_context_lost. After a lost context
  the GPU process is restarted rather than left to recover
  (GpuServiceImpl::MaybeExitOnContextLost). With the GPU in the browser
  process that function returns without doing anything, so there it
  changes nothing; with a separate GPU process it means a restart, and a
  flash, where there was a recovery before.
- 478, gl_vendor ARM and gl_renderer Mali: program binaries are not cached
  for programs that use transform feedback. Harmless beyond a little
  shader compile time.

Entry 93 (GLX indirect rendering, blocks everything) needs a
direct_rendering_version, which nothing sets under EGL, and an empty one
does not match.

Generated for Chromium 154.0.8037.51.

diff --git a/gpu/config/gpu_control_list.cc b/gpu/config/gpu_control_list.cc
--- a/gpu/config/gpu_control_list.cc
+++ b/gpu/config/gpu_control_list.cc
@@ -839,6 +839,13 @@ GpuControlList::OsType GpuControlList::GetOsType() {
   return kOsFuchsia;
 #elif BUILDFLAG(IS_LINUX) || BUILDFLAG(IS_OPENBSD)
   return kOsLinux;
+#elif BUILDFLAG(IS_OHOS)
+  // Trial: the Linux entries, rather than none. With no arm here OHOS fell
+  // through to kOsAny, and every entry that names an operating system was
+  // inert. Of the Linux ones only two can match a Mali device: 283
+  // (exit_on_context_lost) and 478 (no program caching for transform
+  // feedback); the rest are keyed to desktop vendors and drivers.
+  return kOsLinux;
 #elif BUILDFLAG(IS_MAC)
   return kOsMacosx;
 #elif BUILDFLAG(IS_IOS)
